35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The monitors show a four-to-one spread. The template, however, requires keying in every invoice manually. That is not a system; it is a punishment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, forty minutes of logging and arguing? That is way too much! I want a system that takes five minutes, not an evening.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the manual entry is a burden. I found the rooms were assigned by lot, which explains the heating disparity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, the variance is brutal. February was nearly three times August. I need to know if the template can handle that swing without manual entry.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, I saw the other house took forty minutes. That is so long. I hope we can find a way that is gentle and quick for everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the template cannot handle that swing without manual entry. It is a dead end. We need a method that accounts for the four-to-one spread automatically, not one that forces us to log every kilowatt-hour by hand.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I agree! If the template is a dead end, we need something simpler. Maybe we just split the big shared costs evenly and let the monitors handle the rest?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, that sounds reasonable. The lot assignment explains the heating gap, so a flat split for shared costs might be fairer than trying to track every degree.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I agree the template is flawed. But I also saw three late payments caused by shifting amounts. We need stability, not just simplicity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I saw those late payments too. It made the air feel heavy. I want a way that keeps us close, not just on time.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, a flat split ignores the four-to-one reality. We need a hybrid: fixed base for shared, variable for personal. @Jonathan, does the lot assignment justify a permanent premium for the cold room?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, a permanent premium sounds unfair! Maybe we rotate who pays the extra for the cold room each season? That way, no one feels stuck with the burden forever.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, rotating the premium might feel fair, but it adds complexity. I prefer a fixed adjustment based on the heating data we have.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, a fixed adjustment is stable, but I need to know the exact yen amount before I agree. I cannot commit to a number I have not seen.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I understand needing the exact number. But I worry that if the amount changes, we might feel distant again. Can we keep it steady?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the fixed adjustment is roughly two thousand yen monthly. It is stable, predictable, and avoids the chaos of rotation. Let us lock it in.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, two thousand yen sounds manageable! But who actually calculates that every month? I really do not want it to become a huge time sink for anyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the adjustment is a one-time calculation based on the heating data. It does not require monthly recalculation. The base split remains simple.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, two thousand yen is a start, but I need to see how that interacts with the winter spike. I will check the winter habits to understand the peak costs.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, I hope the steady number helps us feel safe. I just want us to smile when we talk about the bills, not hide.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
